# Keep the Docker build context small and clean (see docs/concepts/docker-fundamentals.md §6).
# The whole repo root is the build context (multi-module reactor), so exclude everything that
# isn't needed to compile + package, and anything that would leak host artifacts into the image.

# Build output — the image rebuilds the jar from source inside the Maven stage; we never want
# host-built jars/classes shipped in (they may be stale or built on a different JDK).
**/target/

# Version control + IDE/editor cruft — irrelevant to the build, just bloats the context.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project

# The Maven wrapper jar is downloaded on first use; the build doesn't need a committed copy.
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# Docker + docs + local env — not inputs to the application build.
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
docs/
*.md
.env
